**Aim:** To find the Kth smallest element using the Median of Medians algorithm.

**Pseudocode:**

1. Start.
2. Read array A and K.
3. If the array contains at most five elements, sort it and return the Kth element.
4. Divide the array into groups of five elements.
5. Sort each group and find its median.
6. Find the median of all group medians.
7. Select the median as the pivot.
8. Divide the array into smaller, equal, and greater elements.
9. If K is in the smaller part, recursively search the smaller part.
10. If K is in the equal part, return the pivot.
11. Otherwise, search the greater part with adjusted K.
12. Display the Kth smallest element.
13. Stop.

**Time Complexity:** O(n)

**Space Complexity:** O(n)
**Aim:** To find a subset whose sum equals the target using the Meet-in-the-Middle technique.

**Pseudocode:**

1. Start.
2. Read array A and target sum T.
3. Divide the array into two halves.
4. Generate all possible subset sums of the first half.
5. Generate all possible subset sums of the second half.
6. Sort both lists of subset sums.
7. Initialize one pointer at the beginning of the first list.
8. Initialize another pointer at the end of the second list.
9. Calculate the sum of the two selected subset sums.
10. If the sum equals T, return the combined subset.
11. If the sum is smaller than T, move the first pointer forward.
12. Otherwise, move the second pointer backward.
13. Display the matching subset or report no subset found.
14. Stop.

**Time Complexity:** O(n × 2^(n/2))

**Space Complexity:** O(n × 2^(n/2)) for the given implementation.
